"score":215,"comments":62,"year":2025},{"title":"A sunscreen scandal shocking Australia","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=45145624","site":"Hacker News","score":137,"comments":124,"year":2025},{"title":"Is sunscreen the new margarine? (2019)","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48715020","site":"Hacker News","score":118,"comments":138,"year":2026},{"title":"FDA allows popular sunscreen ingredient long used in Europe and Asia","url":"https://lemmy.world/post/47975203","site":"Lemmy · upliftingnews","score":188,"comments":23,"year":2026},{"title":"After two hours zinc oxide sunscreen loses effectiveness, becomes toxic: study","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=28864619","site":"Hacker News","score":127,"comments":81,"year":2021},{"title":"FDA allows popular sunscreen ingredient long used in Europe and Asia","url":"https://lemmy.world/post/47995907","site":"Lemmy · science","score":183,"comments":16,"year":2026},{"title":"A decades-old FDA rule is keeping Americans from having better sunscreen","url":"https://lemmy.world/post/15047195","site":"Lemmy · health","score":169,"comments":20,"year":2024},{"title":"Is Sunscreen the New Margarine? (2019)","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=23086211","site":"Hacker News","score":74,"comments":82,"year":2020},{"title":"I applied for a job at the sunscreen factory, but I didn't get it.","url":"https://lemmy.world/post/19401707","site":"Lemmy · dadjokes","score":147,"comments":3,"year":2024},{"title":"Fungi found on coconut husks can decompose plastic, sunscreen","url":"https://slrpnk.net/post/38133302","site":"Lemmy · solarpunk","score":144,"comments":2,"year":2026},{"title":"4 things to know about the new sunscreen ingredient the FDA approved","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48523203","site":"Hacker News","score":99,"comments":46,"year":2026},{"title":"Free sunscreen","url":"https://lemmy.world/post/48324337","site":"Lemmy · mildlyinteresting","score":122,"comments":17,"year":2026},{"title":"What should you do if you get rejected for a job at the sunscreen factory?","url":"https://lemmy.ml/post/16978003","site":"Lemmy · dadjokes","score":114,"comments":3,"year":2024},{"title":"Low Fat Diet and Sunscreen: a Recipe for Disaster","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=330981","site":"Hacker News","score":47,"comments":59,"year":2008},{"title":"Is Sunscreen a Lifesaver or a Poison?","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=8168085","site":"Hacker News","score":44,"comments":61,"year":2014},{"title":"Ask HN: Are You Wearing Sunscreen?","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=32378059","site":"Hacker News","score":27,"comments":59,"year":2022},{"title":"Sunscreen Worries Grow as Another Potential Carcinogen Found","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=28129689","site":"Hacker News","score":38,"comments":20,"year":2021},{"title":"Sunscreen enters bloodstream after just one day of use","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=19843762","site":"Hacker News","score":40,"comments":16,"year":2019}],"web":[{"title":"Sunscreen - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunscreen"},{"title":"Vitamin C - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vitamin_C"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Skin","chain":["Vitamin C serum applied first","Sunscreen layered on top","Brighter, better-protected skin"],"effect":"indirect","text":"A vitamin C serum under sunscreen each morning pairs an antioxidant with UV filters for brighter, better-protected skin. Each product's role is known; the pairing itself has not been trialled."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["The sunscreen and vitamin C layering routine is a daytime skincare habit in which a topical vitamin C (ascorbic acid or a derivative) serum is applied first and a broad-spectrum sunscreen is applied over it. It is commonly described as a brightening and anti-ageing routine.","Wikipedia's sunscreen article states that antioxidants, including ascorbic acid and its derivatives, can interact with UV filters to affect photostability and reduce reactive oxygen species, depending on formulation, and describes antioxidants as a second line of defence behind the UV filters [1]. Several of those statements carry citation-needed tags on that page, and no specific trial of the layering routine appears in the sources consulted."],"infobox":[["Type","Daytime skincare routine"],["Components","Topical vitamin C serum plus broad-spectrum sunscreen"],["Goals","Brightening, photoprotection, anti-ageing"],["Prescription needed","No"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["The routine pairs two products: an antioxidant serum, applied after cleansing, and sunscreen as the final daytime step. Sunscreens work by absorbing, reflecting or scattering UV light, using mineral filters such as zinc oxide and titanium dioxide, organic filters, or both [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Background on the components","paras":["Wikipedia reports that sun protection factor (SPF) measures the fraction of sunburn-causing UVB reaching skin, that reapplication is generally advised about every two hours, and that people often apply less than the tested amount [1]. It reports that daily sunscreen use was associated with smoother skin in a 2013 Australian study of about 900 people [1].","Vitamin C was discovered in 1912, isolated in 1928 and in 1933 became the first vitamin to be chemically synthesised [2]. Wikipedia's vitamin C article describes it as a cofactor in collagen formation, as a scavenger of reactive oxygen species, and as highly prone to oxidation, a point that article makes in the context of food [2]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found of the layering routine as such. Wikipedia's sunscreen article cites figures on antioxidants improving reactive-oxygen-species suppression in sunscreen formulations, but these are formulation-dependent findings, not trials of the routine [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"In looksmaxxing culture","paras":["The routine is described as a standard brightening step in skincare circles. Proponents say vitamin C adds antioxidant protection beneath sunscreen and evens skin tone."],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"Community discussion treats vitamin C under sunscreen as a standard morning step.","claims":[{"claim":"Vitamin C under sunscreen adds extra protection against sun damage","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"The routine brightens skin","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[{"year":"1912","event":"Vitamin C is discovered [2]."},{"year":"1974","event":"Franz Greiter introduces the SPF rating [1]."}],"refs":[{"title":"Sunscreen","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunscreen","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Vitamin C","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vitamin_C","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Sunscreen","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunscreen","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Sunscreen Ruins My Face","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/sunscreen-ruins-my-face.514290/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220926000416/https://looksmax.org/threads/sunscreen-ruins-my-face.514290/"},{"title":"Guide Sunscreen, and why should you use","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/sunscreen-and-why-should-you-use.369349/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210704161605/https://looksmax.org/threads/sunscreen-and-why-should-you-use.369349/"},{"title":"Serious Sunscreen recommendations","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/sunscreen-recommendations.307512/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230626074953/https://looksmax.org/threads/sunscreen-recommendations.307512/"},{"title":"sunscreen and prevention of skin aging","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/sunscreen-and-prevention-of-skin-aging.29429/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20210713051122/https://looksmax